From 78724c4aaf81d847a946e9761a9168ac529f383c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:35:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 30/31] Binding test on the debug page

Fix round 2, B6 and the phone figures of A2/A4 (debug and profile builds
only, BuildConfig.LIVENESS_DIAGNOSTICS).

Face binding test card:
- 1. Binding gate: a real Resident face gate; its best frame stays held
  natively.
- 2. Capture still and bind: Pigeon captureStill(camera, jp2) takes the
  15th camera frame (exposure settled), without liveness and without a
  preview, as JPEG or, when ticked, JPEG 2000 (the SBI format, so the JP2
  decoder is exercised). bindCapturedFace then compares it with the held
  best frame. Neither image is shown or logged; the page shows the
  outcome, the similarity and the threshold in a snack bar and in the card.
- Matcher benchmark: Pigeon runMatcherBenchmark(camera) captures 20 frames
  into memory and runs MatcherBenchmark (liveness module) on the last two
  with exactly one face, for the bundled models and each signed test
  bundle in files/bench-bundles/: a fresh factory's preload, the first
  comparison without warm-up, warmUpMatcher and the first comparison
  after it, warm comparisons and the one-face embedding p50. The report
  has timings and the outcome only; the frames are dropped.
- LivenessApi.captureFrames: the shared camera capture (refused while a
  session or a benchmark runs). LivenessServiceHolder.runMatcherBenchmark.

Live, phone S23 FE, debug build (the tester's face in the gate):
- pad-2026.10.4 (fp32): the tester in the still MATCH 0.92; a NASA
  portrait on the laptop screen NO_MATCH 0.15; an empty wall NO_FACE_B.
- pad-2026.10.5 (int8): the tester MATCH 0.90, in 353 ms.
- Matcher benchmark, fp32 / int8 (pad-2026.10.95, a local test bundle):
  one-face embedding p50 45.6 / 36.8 ms; warm comparison 128 / 76 ms;
  warmUpMatcher 35 / 38 ms; the first comparison without warm-up 203 /
  140 ms, after it 89 / 75 ms.

MatcherBenchmarkTest: frames without a face are skipped (MATCH on the two
faces), too few faces say so, no similarity in the report.

